# Internal QA working doc — paranoid paper/supplement↔monograph fact-check
# (2026-06-12). Working artifact, not part of the publication; kept out of the
# soon-public history. Delete or fold into the audit ledger when resolved.
audit/factcheck_paper_supplement_vs_monograph.md

# Sensitive internal review material — NEVER publish (repo will be made public).
# Supervisor/co-author annotated feedback + internal authorship/review to-do
# notes. Scoped to these SPECIFIC files only — deliberately NOT wildcards, so
# nothing legitimate is ever ignored by accident. To protect a new sensitive
# file, add its exact name here AND to the guard list in .githooks/pre-commit.
#
# This literal-only rule is HALF of a two-tier design (2026-07-28). The other
# half is .githooks/pre-commit, which DOES use broad patterns (TODO_*.md,
# ROADMAP_*.md, NEXT_SESSION*.md). The asymmetry is deliberate and the two files
# are not meant to converge: an over-broad .gitignore fails SILENTLY (a
# legitimate file is swallowed and never published, and nobody notices), whereas
# an over-broad commit guard fails LOUDLY (the commit stops with an explanation
# and a human decides). So breadth belongs in the guard, not here. See the long
# comment at the top of .githooks/pre-commit before changing either.
Paper_retour_PJ.pdf
paper_feedback_michaelSauthier.docx
TODO_PJ_feedback.md
TODO_yassir_track.md
TODO_publication_roadmap.md
# Internal reviewer-prep rebuttal working doc (2026-07-07). Deploy only if a
# reviewer challenges the Morris screening design; never part of the publication.
internal_morris_rebuttal.md

# Firecrawl CLI local cache (2026-07-28). The tool writes .firecrawl/ into the
# working directory, and it flagged itself that the folder was untracked-but-not-
# ignored here. Scraped pages are third-party content fetched for verification;
# they are working material, not repository content. Literal name, as above.
.firecrawl/

# Closed-access primary sources kept locally so a challenged citation can be
# reopened instead of re-requested (2026-07-28). Paywalled articles and textbook
# scans: redistributing them through a public Apache-2.0 repository would be a
# copyright violation, quite separate from the licence covering our own work.
# The folder's own README states the rules; the verbatim extracts that actually
# carry evidential weight live in audit/reference_audit.md, not here.
# Literal folder name, per the two-tier design documented above.
local_sources/

# Local handoff folder (endorsement review copies) — not part of the repo
for_endorsement/

# Pre-submission inquiry draft (prep aid, not part of the submission package yet)
preprint_npj/pre_submission_inquiry.txt

# Internal working audit — not for publication until its findings are resolved
audit/monograph_comprehensibility_audit.md

